WEBVTT

00:29.112 --> 00:30.197
IN YOUR RADIANT SEASON

00:33.283 --> 00:34.909
CHARACTERS, EVENTS, ORGANIZATIONS,
AND PLACES IN THIS DRAMA ARE FICTITIOUS

00:34.910 --> 00:36.203
ALL CHILD ACTORS AND ANIMALS
FILMED IN A SAFE ENVIRONMENT

00:36.787 --> 00:37.870
Mr. Park.

00:37.871 --> 00:40.666
Mr. Park, did you see…

00:49.174 --> 00:50.466
I can't reach him.

00:50.467 --> 00:52.636
He took his car and left

00:53.804 --> 00:55.264
after 2:00 a.m. last night.

00:56.306 --> 00:57.723
He has a bad fever.

00:57.724 --> 00:59.850
He's not in a state to drive right now.

00:59.851 --> 01:01.769
Then I should call the police--

01:01.770 --> 01:02.771
Seonu Chan!

01:04.564 --> 01:07.024
- Ben.
- Is he here?

01:07.025 --> 01:09.027
I haven't been able to reach him.

01:09.736 --> 01:11.612
Why? Is something wrong?

01:11.613 --> 01:14.324
He sent an email to the headquarters

01:14.950 --> 01:16.534
saying he'll quit.

01:16.535 --> 01:17.618
What?

01:17.619 --> 01:19.036
I can't get in touch with him,

01:19.037 --> 01:21.790
and they said he even deleted
his email account already.

01:23.041 --> 01:24.543
He must have vanished on purpose.

01:25.127 --> 01:26.461
Goodness.

01:34.928 --> 01:36.763
He's been planning it
for a long time.

01:37.347 --> 01:40.224
He said he wanted to be with you

01:40.225 --> 01:41.935
through spring, summer, fall, and winter.

01:42.394 --> 01:44.771
He said he'd explain everything soon.

01:47.107 --> 01:49.818
But it looks like
it's broken beyond repair.

01:50.861 --> 01:52.029
He was hesitant

01:53.655 --> 01:55.907
because his memories weren't fully intact.

01:56.742 --> 01:59.035
And he was worried that

01:59.036 --> 02:02.039
acting rashly would only hurt you.

02:02.789 --> 02:04.708
He was going through a hard time too,

02:06.418 --> 02:09.338
but his mind was only focused on you.

02:11.131 --> 02:14.468
But it seems like
he missed several chances to tell you.

02:15.427 --> 02:17.595
There was that issue
with your grandma too.

02:19.556 --> 02:20.557
I…

02:23.310 --> 02:24.895
made him leave.

02:25.437 --> 02:27.438
You don't have to look at me
or listen to me.

02:27.439 --> 02:28.649
Please, just look at this.

02:29.900 --> 02:31.067
So please…

02:31.068 --> 02:33.362
No exceptions.
Don't let anyone in my office.

02:34.946 --> 02:37.114
Don't ever show up in front of me again.

02:37.115 --> 02:39.700
You just pushed me back into winter again.

02:39.701 --> 02:42.079
I should have listened to him at least.

02:42.871 --> 02:44.164
What do I do?

02:45.624 --> 02:48.251
Regardless of whose roommate
he was seven years ago,

02:50.212 --> 02:52.172
what secrets he hid…

02:55.217 --> 02:57.594
or what he did wrong,

02:59.680 --> 03:01.515
I really can't hate him.

03:35.132 --> 03:37.384
I'm only visiting.
I came from Boston.
:cue

03:50.230 --> 03:51.897
END OF TRIAL

03:54.943 --> 03:56.193
A three-month trial!

03:56.194 --> 03:59.488
As soon as the three months is over,
I'll disappear without a trace.

03:59.489 --> 04:01.616
I'm not someone who will leave
in three months,

04:02.742 --> 04:04.869
nor someone who might never come back.

04:04.870 --> 04:06.163
Ms. Song.

04:06.746 --> 04:09.498
No, Haran. I want to stay with you.

04:09.499 --> 04:13.170
I'm going to use that trial
for the rest of my life.

04:14.754 --> 04:16.882
When did he come here?

04:22.637 --> 04:24.139
Where did you go, Seonu Chan?

04:30.187 --> 04:32.354
Then that accident…

04:32.355 --> 04:34.857
Yes. It was all because of you.

04:34.858 --> 04:37.736
You caused the accident,
and it killed Hyeokchan.

04:49.122 --> 04:50.123
He…

04:50.999 --> 04:52.042
disappeared.

04:53.877 --> 04:57.672
The Seonu Chan I know
would never just leave like that.

04:58.965 --> 05:01.134
I'm sure there must be a reason.

05:02.594 --> 05:04.554
But I didn't even give him
a chance to talk.

05:05.555 --> 05:06.765
So I'm regretting it.

05:10.352 --> 05:12.979
You, he, and Hyeokchan knew each other

05:13.688 --> 05:14.773
in Boston, right?

05:17.442 --> 05:18.568
Yes.

05:20.362 --> 05:21.862
His disappearance

05:21.863 --> 05:24.324
seems to be connected
to what happened seven years ago.

05:25.492 --> 05:27.285
What happened back then?

05:28.328 --> 05:29.329
Please tell me.

05:29.955 --> 05:31.248
I have to know.

05:34.209 --> 05:35.293
I'm sorry.

05:36.837 --> 05:38.046
Seven years ago,

05:39.130 --> 05:41.049
I did something bad to you.

05:43.385 --> 05:46.012
I met Hyeokchan for the first time
at a hospital.

05:47.389 --> 05:51.183
He and I were both waiting for a surgery.

05:51.184 --> 05:53.144
He was pretty stressed back then

05:53.895 --> 05:56.189
because he couldn't reach you often.

05:58.191 --> 05:59.192
What time is it?

05:59.901 --> 06:03.362
I missed his calls again.

06:05.365 --> 06:07.658
Did you download it?
Can you see my message?

06:07.659 --> 06:09.035
Yes, I can see it!

06:09.786 --> 06:11.161
You kept missing my calls,

06:11.162 --> 06:14.916
so I thought we could at least
send each other messages on our laptops.

06:17.919 --> 06:20.337
I'm going to bed now. Love you.

06:20.338 --> 06:22.256
Oh, no…

06:22.257 --> 06:24.383
The silk georgette…

06:24.384 --> 06:26.969
- Haran, the draping fabric.
-  Coming.

06:26.970 --> 06:28.429
Sorry, I'm in a bit of a hurry.

06:28.430 --> 06:30.098
I'll call you back later. Sorry.

06:34.519 --> 06:36.146
You shouldn't be smoking.

06:37.814 --> 06:38.815
None of your business.

06:39.733 --> 06:40.734
Are you Korean?

06:46.031 --> 06:48.240
Let's meet up and chat from time to time.

06:48.241 --> 06:49.826
We're both lonely students here.

06:52.912 --> 06:54.371
We were the same age,

06:54.372 --> 06:56.915
and we were both lonely students
studying abroad.

06:56.916 --> 06:58.876
So we grew close quickly.

07:02.339 --> 07:04.381
You were the only one
who could bring this.

07:04.382 --> 07:07.259
But I didn't have your number,
so I asked the T.A.

07:07.260 --> 07:09.054
Sorry for the hassle.

07:14.517 --> 07:15.601
My number.

07:15.602 --> 07:17.854
Call me if you need anything.
Not too often, though.
:cue

07:22.442 --> 07:24.485
Sorry.

07:24.486 --> 07:26.612
I heard
he wasn't close with his roommate,

07:26.613 --> 07:28.864
but he asked Seonu Chan for a favor,

07:28.865 --> 07:30.532
and that's when I first met him.

07:30.533 --> 07:33.494
- Who's that? Your friend?
- No, just my roommate.

07:36.665 --> 07:40.417
We developed feelings
for each other as we grew close.

07:42.671 --> 07:45.005
We kept seeing each other
after we were discharged.

07:45.006 --> 07:47.466
That's when Hyeokchan
started making excuses

07:47.467 --> 07:49.594
and asking his roommate for favors.

07:50.303 --> 07:52.346
He canceled his plans to go to Korea

07:52.347 --> 07:54.390
and went traveling with me
during vacation,

07:54.391 --> 07:57.226
but he accidentally took
his roommate's laptop instead.

07:57.227 --> 07:58.812
And during that one month,

08:00.563 --> 08:03.191
I think Seonu Chan was chatting

08:04.526 --> 08:05.777
with you

08:06.403 --> 08:07.529
on Hyeokchan's laptop.

08:08.446 --> 08:12.574
Hyeokchan had already made up his mind
to break up with you.

08:12.575 --> 08:14.369
I'm sorry, but the reason was me.

08:16.579 --> 08:19.165
Seonu Chan didn't start it intentionally.

08:19.874 --> 08:23.544
It was Hyeokchan's mistake,
and he asked him to message you.

08:24.629 --> 08:26.881
Did you have fun
chatting with me like that?

08:27.757 --> 08:30.468
Did you build some kind of fantasy
and start liking me?

08:32.011 --> 08:33.596
Even though I knew about you,

08:35.473 --> 08:36.850
I wanted Hyeokchan.

08:38.268 --> 08:39.269
I'm sorry.

08:44.482 --> 08:45.984
All right.

08:50.822 --> 08:52.198
Seonu Chan…

08:53.533 --> 08:54.993
disappeared because of me.

09:00.123 --> 09:02.541
If his bleeding
was caused by the shrapnel,

09:02.542 --> 09:04.168
it may be accompanied

09:04.169 --> 09:06.670
by neurological symptoms
such as auditory or visual hallucinations.

09:06.671 --> 09:09.381
There have even been reports
of memory distortion

09:09.382 --> 09:11.258
in severe cases like this.

09:11.259 --> 09:13.136
Memory distortion?

09:13.845 --> 09:16.013
His memories are distorted?

09:16.014 --> 09:17.306
I had no idea

09:17.307 --> 09:20.642
he'd been suffering so much
from the explosion back then.

09:20.643 --> 09:25.398
He told me never to tell you
about Hyeokchan and me,

09:25.940 --> 09:27.775
but I thought I should tell you.

09:27.776 --> 09:29.360
I get that about Hyeokchan,

09:29.986 --> 09:31.154
but what do you mean?

09:31.821 --> 09:32.905
Why did he disappear--

09:32.906 --> 09:34.783
I did something…

09:35.992 --> 09:38.703
I shouldn't have done,
as a person and as a doctor.

09:51.633 --> 09:52.883
Your passport? Why?

09:52.884 --> 09:54.635
I'm going to Boston to meet Chan,

09:54.636 --> 09:56.178
since we have four days off.

09:56.179 --> 09:57.806
What? Really?

09:58.640 --> 10:00.557
You seem different these days.

10:00.558 --> 10:01.892
What? Why?

10:01.893 --> 10:05.729
Just a while back,
you didn't seem that into him.

10:05.730 --> 10:07.189
Was that a month ago?

10:07.190 --> 10:09.400
What's this sudden burst of affection?

10:10.276 --> 10:11.361
I don't know, either.

10:11.820 --> 10:14.863
When we were together,
I didn't notice him much,

10:14.864 --> 10:17.825
but I feel like I can see him clearer
when I'm chatting with him

10:17.826 --> 10:19.202
without seeing or hearing him.

10:19.744 --> 10:23.540
I can tell how much he understands me
and how well we click.

10:24.374 --> 10:27.668
Maybe it's because of this pen.

10:30.797 --> 10:31.923
What do I do?

10:36.219 --> 10:37.262
What do I do?

10:39.514 --> 10:42.642
What do I do?

10:53.444 --> 10:55.445
IN YOUR RADIANT SEASON
:cue

10:57.365 --> 10:58.700
Mr. Yeon.

10:59.951 --> 11:01.410
I'm going to the factory.

11:01.411 --> 11:05.372
I'm meeting Mr. Chae
in front of the factory at 4:00 p.m.

11:05.373 --> 11:09.043
I heard it's in Gangwon-do Province.
It's pretty far, so drive safely.

11:11.087 --> 11:14.131
But what happened to your keychain?

11:14.132 --> 11:16.425
Oh, I'm taking the company car
since it's far away.

11:16.426 --> 11:19.386
Ah. Sorry, I can't come with you.

11:19.387 --> 11:21.763
No need to apologize for that.

11:21.764 --> 11:24.725
I know you're insanely busy
with Ms. Kim absent.

11:24.726 --> 11:26.895
I'll see you later, then.

11:31.482 --> 11:33.193
It's going to take so long.

11:36.070 --> 11:38.030
I have to cheer him up.

11:39.824 --> 11:40.825
Smile.

11:45.705 --> 11:46.706
Huh?

11:50.210 --> 11:51.211
"Kim."

11:55.506 --> 11:56.674
YOUGYUM

12:01.638 --> 12:03.681
Why isn't he picking up?

12:10.396 --> 12:12.940
Yang Changmo.
Do you know where Yougyum is?

12:12.941 --> 12:15.025
He's taking his stuff
out of his locker.

12:15.026 --> 12:16.444
He says he's quitting baseball.

12:17.237 --> 12:18.737
- What?
- He said

12:18.738 --> 12:21.115
he won't be able to become
a pro athlete anyway.

12:30.083 --> 12:31.125
CHA YOUGYUM

12:45.598 --> 12:47.182
In 2007,

12:47.183 --> 12:49.518
Park Jisung got knee surgery

12:49.519 --> 12:52.187
and returned to Manchester United
after nine months.

12:52.188 --> 12:54.274
He made it
to the Champions League semifinals.

12:59.237 --> 13:01.029
In 2025,

13:01.030 --> 13:04.616
Shohei Ohtani returned
from two elbow surgeries

13:04.617 --> 13:06.285
and threw even faster than before,

13:06.286 --> 13:09.037
rewriting his Major League career records.

13:09.038 --> 13:10.581
And in 2015,

13:11.165 --> 13:12.583
Ryu Hyunjin…

13:14.460 --> 13:15.795
had a shoulder tear…

13:16.546 --> 13:17.547
Shoulder tear…

13:20.174 --> 13:21.175
Hadam, stop.

13:22.552 --> 13:23.553
That's enough.

13:24.721 --> 13:25.722
I'm sorry.

13:27.473 --> 13:28.808
I'm really sorry,

13:29.726 --> 13:30.810
but I can't make it.

13:32.145 --> 13:33.396
Those athletes

13:34.272 --> 13:36.691
took much longer to recover than expected.

13:37.817 --> 13:39.193
But they returned stronger.

13:40.194 --> 13:42.487
You don't have to play baseball.

13:42.488 --> 13:44.948
And you don't have to join
the Major League.

13:44.949 --> 13:46.034
But…

13:46.743 --> 13:49.077
if you give up now
without trying until the end,

13:49.078 --> 13:50.455
all you can do later…

13:52.290 --> 13:53.374
is regret it.

13:55.084 --> 13:57.003
Let's try everything we can until the end.

13:57.503 --> 13:58.963
You can give up then.

13:59.922 --> 14:01.924
Until you find something else
you want to do,

14:03.092 --> 14:04.718
I'll take care of you, so--

14:04.719 --> 14:05.720
I'm scared.

14:08.723 --> 14:11.893
I'm scared I'll turn out to be nothing
even after I try.

14:15.980 --> 14:16.981
Then,

14:17.815 --> 14:19.859
you can be the Cha Yougyum

14:20.902 --> 14:23.029
who at least tried his best until the end.

14:23.654 --> 14:24.655
You can be that.

14:25.448 --> 14:27.949
Then you won't turn out to be nothing.

14:27.950 --> 14:29.494
You helped me stay strong

14:30.620 --> 14:32.205
when I was having a rough time.

14:33.706 --> 14:35.708
So it's my turn to help you stand back up.

14:36.167 --> 14:39.294
Even if you give up baseball,
I won't let go of your hand.

14:39.295 --> 14:40.963
I'll stay with you until the end.

14:44.175 --> 14:45.301
So let's not…

14:46.844 --> 14:47.970
run away from this.

14:55.228 --> 14:56.229
I'll give it a try.

14:57.647 --> 15:00.483
We can cry later if I still can't do it.

15:00.942 --> 15:02.276
But right now,

15:04.112 --> 15:05.113
let's try this.

15:13.788 --> 15:14.789
REPORTER CHAE HYUNWOO

15:15.331 --> 15:16.957
- Yes, Mr. Chae.
-  Hey.

15:16.958 --> 15:19.543
We rescheduled the factory visit
to next Wednesday.

15:19.544 --> 15:20.669
Can you join us then?

15:20.670 --> 15:21.921
What are you talking about?

15:22.547 --> 15:24.756
Ms. Song just left for Yeongwol.
:cue

15:24.757 --> 15:27.843
Huh? I left her a message
saying it got canceled.

15:27.844 --> 15:30.513
We can't enter
because of a blizzard warning.

15:32.473 --> 15:34.308
MR. YEON

15:37.186 --> 15:41.982
Hello, this is Song Hayeong's phone
that she leaves lying around every day.

15:48.489 --> 15:49.823
Chae Hyunwoo.

15:49.824 --> 15:52.784
You should've checked
to see if she got the message.

15:55.746 --> 15:57.122
Send me the address.

16:01.502 --> 16:02.586
I'm sorry.

16:02.587 --> 16:05.673
Something urgent came up,
so I have to postpone the meeting.

16:06.924 --> 16:08.426
I'm really sorry.

16:17.310 --> 16:20.354
I can't believe this.

16:20.897 --> 16:21.898
What is this?

16:23.065 --> 16:24.066
Huh?

16:26.194 --> 16:28.779
This is driving me crazy.

16:33.201 --> 16:35.994
You can't enter
because of the heavy snow.

16:35.995 --> 16:38.539
You have to head back, all right?

16:41.918 --> 16:43.376
Hang on.

16:43.377 --> 16:44.586
Excuse me.

16:44.587 --> 16:46.130
You can't enter. Excuse me!

16:46.923 --> 16:49.257
Sir! Wait!

16:51.427 --> 16:55.139
My car won't start,
and I don't even have my phone.

16:56.515 --> 16:58.851
It's so cold.

17:01.020 --> 17:04.649
You can't fall asleep,
Song Hayeong.

17:05.149 --> 17:07.068
Am I going to die here?

17:08.736 --> 17:09.779
Well…

17:10.529 --> 17:13.032
I've lived a happy life.

17:13.658 --> 17:16.369
I was so stupid.

17:17.453 --> 17:18.871
Ms. Song Hayeong.

17:19.872 --> 17:21.164
Ms. Song!

17:21.165 --> 17:24.292
Why am I hallucinating Mr. Yeon's voice
in a moment like this?

17:28.923 --> 17:29.924
Huh?

17:32.051 --> 17:33.970
Mr. Yeon?

17:36.973 --> 17:37.974
Ms. Song.

17:39.725 --> 17:41.102
Are you all right?

17:41.561 --> 17:43.729
Is that really you, Mr. Yeon?

17:44.730 --> 17:45.773
Yes, it's me.

17:48.859 --> 17:49.986
Everything's okay now.

17:53.072 --> 17:55.992
I'll call a car service right away.
Just a moment.

17:59.453 --> 18:00.454
Wow.

18:11.757 --> 18:14.009
I'm fine, so take this…

18:14.010 --> 18:15.052
No.

18:15.720 --> 18:18.138
Keep it on.

18:18.139 --> 18:21.058
Don't make me get the wrong idea again.

18:21.517 --> 18:25.562
You would've rushed over
even if it were Haran or Hadam, right?

18:31.152 --> 18:32.528
I'm not sure.

18:33.904 --> 18:34.905
What?

18:37.158 --> 18:38.618
I think I was wrong.

18:39.410 --> 18:40.535
What…

18:40.536 --> 18:41.704
I think I do see you…

18:43.664 --> 18:45.124
as more than a colleague.

18:54.925 --> 18:57.261
I told myself I couldn't dare to,

18:58.596 --> 19:00.181
since you're Ms. Kim's granddaughter.

19:02.391 --> 19:06.145
So I guess I turned away from my feelings.

19:10.858 --> 19:12.860
How could I not be attracted

19:14.528 --> 19:17.823
to someone like you?

19:21.369 --> 19:22.787
I know it's pretty late,

19:23.704 --> 19:27.208
but if you're really okay
with someone like me…

19:32.338 --> 19:33.756
would it be all right

19:35.216 --> 19:36.425
for me to like you?
:cue

19:54.026 --> 19:55.069
Gosh…

19:55.611 --> 19:57.697
Let's clean up this place

19:58.739 --> 20:00.991
so Chan can return anytime.

20:29.478 --> 20:30.563
Yes?

20:32.106 --> 20:34.066
Ms. Song, there's a delivery for you.

20:47.037 --> 20:48.330
Have you been well?

20:48.914 --> 20:50.458
It took a while,

20:51.083 --> 20:52.960
but I put it together.

20:57.840 --> 21:02.928
Restoration begins the moment
you decide to put it back together.

21:03.429 --> 21:04.721
It may take a while,

21:04.722 --> 21:08.893
but as long as you don't give up,
the pieces will come together in the end,

21:09.393 --> 21:10.936
and those pieces

21:11.520 --> 21:14.023
will contain a deeper story
compared to before.

21:14.565 --> 21:16.484
I learned through this job

21:17.526 --> 21:21.447
that miracles begin by not giving up.

21:22.114 --> 21:24.784
If there is anything you wish to fix,

21:25.493 --> 21:30.164
I hope a miracle occurs for you as well.

21:31.540 --> 21:33.501
Not giving up…

21:55.940 --> 21:58.691
The service center refused
since the model is discontinued.

21:58.692 --> 22:00.235
Will you be able to fix it?

22:00.236 --> 22:03.154
I could try if I had new parts for this,

22:03.155 --> 22:07.368
but it'll be hard since this model
was sold briefly over 10 years ago.

22:07.868 --> 22:08.869
I'm sorry.

22:11.372 --> 22:14.332
Would anyone
be able to fix this drawing pad?

22:14.333 --> 22:16.836
I'll repay anyone
who can at least recover the data.

22:20.047 --> 22:22.173
What's this? An old tablet?

22:22.174 --> 22:23.801
A drawing pad like this exists?

22:30.724 --> 22:33.017
Wow,
I used this in middle school.

22:33.018 --> 22:34.812
It's probably stashed somewhere.

22:36.647 --> 22:38.648
I could try
if I had new parts for this.

22:41.402 --> 22:44.612
Are you willing
to sell it to me if you find it?

22:44.613 --> 22:47.032
If you are, please message me.

22:51.620 --> 22:54.039
ARE YOU WILLING
TO SELL IT TO ME IF YOU FIND IT?

23:02.339 --> 23:03.423
Hello?

23:03.424 --> 23:05.925
Are you the one
who left a message saying

23:05.926 --> 23:08.345
- you wanted to buy my drawing pad?
- Yes, I am.

23:09.889 --> 23:12.140
I found a working drawing pad.

23:12.141 --> 23:14.351
The parts are in there,
so you can fix it, right?

23:15.060 --> 23:17.855
I can't guarantee that,
but you can leave it with me.

23:23.485 --> 23:24.986
Thanks to the new parts,

23:24.987 --> 23:28.574
I managed to restore the data
and move it to another device.

23:29.116 --> 23:30.701
to HARAN

23:42.922 --> 23:47.508
1. SUMMER, SEVEN YEARS AGO
IT STARTED WITH WALLS

23:53.599 --> 23:55.016
Hyeokchan and I

23:55.017 --> 23:57.311
were roommates
at the Boston Institute of Technology.

23:57.811 --> 24:00.480
Can you message her back
and say I have to go to the lab?

24:00.481 --> 24:02.024
Do me a solid.

24:05.736 --> 24:08.989
One day, I was about to turn off
Hyeokchan's messenger alarm,

24:09.698 --> 24:11.575
but your words caught my eye.

24:12.451 --> 24:13.786
"Surrounded by walls."

24:14.453 --> 24:16.497
Perhaps because I'd been feeling that way,

24:17.748 --> 24:19.917
I wanted to be someone you could talk to.

24:20.834 --> 24:23.086
I could guess
how lost you would be feeling.

24:23.087 --> 24:24.671
IF IT'S OKAY WITH YOU, YOU CAN TALK TO ME

24:24.672 --> 24:26.715
:cue

24:33.973 --> 24:35.975
All I did was listen to you,

24:36.850 --> 24:39.269
but strangely, it comforted me too.

24:42.773 --> 24:45.359
THANKS FOR LISTENING TO ME COMPLAIN!

24:46.026 --> 24:47.319
I thought

24:47.987 --> 24:50.613
that would be
our first and last conversation.

24:50.614 --> 24:51.907
But…

24:54.076 --> 24:55.702
2. FOUNTAIN PEN, AND ENGRAVING

24:55.703 --> 24:57.871
Around that time,
Hyeokchan hurt his hand badly,

24:58.747 --> 25:00.457
and he asked me for a favor.

25:01.250 --> 25:04.460
Anything that a woman
in her twenties can use.

25:04.461 --> 25:06.295
He wanted to get you a gift,

25:06.296 --> 25:09.133
but he couldn't make time
because of his treatment.

25:09.675 --> 25:11.175
He felt really sorry.

25:11.176 --> 25:14.888
I'm looking for a pen, like…

25:15.931 --> 25:19.393
A pen for efficient design sketches.
Do you have them?

25:19.977 --> 25:22.645
That's when
I remembered what you'd said.

25:22.646 --> 25:26.899
You said you were surrounded by walls
and you couldn't sketch anything.

25:26.900 --> 25:30.486
Hoping it would cheer you up a bit,
I chose a drawing pen.

25:30.487 --> 25:32.072
Okay, I'll take this.

25:32.865 --> 25:36.201
Is it a gift?
I could engrave it if you'd like.

25:41.123 --> 25:42.249
"Haran."

25:42.833 --> 25:44.083
I suddenly remembered

25:44.084 --> 25:47.796
the name Hyeokchan had said
when he was calling you.

25:49.715 --> 25:52.176
The design contest winner is…

25:52.926 --> 25:54.761
Congratulations, Haran.

25:54.762 --> 25:56.180
YOU KNOW, YOU'RE MY SAVIOR.

25:57.431 --> 26:00.726
Hyeokchan was away
to help our professor with some research.

26:02.311 --> 26:05.354
I'm traveling around the East Coast
during vacation.

26:05.355 --> 26:09.151
If our professor asks for me,
say I'm taking a break because of my hand.

26:09.985 --> 26:11.986
Our laptops got switched
by accident back then…

26:13.322 --> 26:16.325
…and soon after,
I had another day where I felt trapped.

26:23.332 --> 26:25.333
How long are you going to keep doing this?

26:25.334 --> 26:28.629
What more do I have to do
to make you stop?

26:30.297 --> 26:32.507
Do you remember

26:32.508 --> 26:36.428
how I said I stood alone
in a harsh winter as well?

26:37.971 --> 26:41.432
I'd been barely holding on,
surrounded by walls,

26:41.433 --> 26:44.352
but just as I was about to give up
and end everything…

26:45.437 --> 26:48.315
…you suddenly spoke to me

26:49.108 --> 26:51.568
right when I was about to die.

26:52.402 --> 26:53.529
"You're…

26:54.655 --> 26:56.072
my savior."

26:56.073 --> 26:58.616
I knew those words weren't meant for me,

26:58.617 --> 27:01.328
but I wanted to cling to them.

27:02.162 --> 27:04.123
You said I was your savior,

27:04.706 --> 27:06.750
but you were the one who saved me.

27:07.835 --> 27:08.836
And that…

27:09.503 --> 27:11.171
gave me reason to keep living.

27:11.797 --> 27:13.132
Song Haran.

27:13.465 --> 27:15.258
You saved me,

27:15.259 --> 27:16.343
seven years ago.

27:17.302 --> 27:18.679
You saved me back then!

27:20.472 --> 27:22.390
Since then…

27:22.391 --> 27:24.643
…I couldn't ignore the messages you sent,

27:25.269 --> 27:26.644
thinking it was Hyeokchan.

27:26.645 --> 27:29.272
GOLDBERG, NEON ALIEN, SMELL OF RAIN
THE PERSON WHO BROADENED MY WORLD

27:30.774 --> 27:33.860
That Gold-something that
helps you sleep. I heard there's no proof.

27:33.861 --> 27:36.070
It's like music to wake you up.

27:38.323 --> 27:40.449
I'd forgotten how to smile,

27:40.450 --> 27:42.619
but I started smiling because of you.

27:44.872 --> 27:46.122
Shocking news.

27:46.123 --> 27:48.541
I was eating lunch,
and there was eggplant in it.

27:48.542 --> 27:49.625
Eggplant?

27:49.626 --> 27:53.212
It's all mushy and squishy,
and it's neon-colored. Yuck!

27:53.213 --> 27:54.464
The taste of a neon alien.

27:55.966 --> 27:57.134
A neon alien…

27:57.551 --> 27:58.801
I grew curious about you...

27:59.887 --> 28:01.138
...and started looking forward

28:02.014 --> 28:04.141
to what interesting stories
you'd tell me next.

28:06.268 --> 28:09.812
My black-and-white life
began to be filled with colors,

28:09.813 --> 28:11.815
and my tiny world

28:12.816 --> 28:14.151
began to grow bigger,

28:14.610 --> 28:17.321
thanks to your messages.

28:18.322 --> 28:21.325
Thank you for helping me
not give up on what I love.

28:21.825 --> 28:23.619
For giving me a reason to keep going.

28:25.454 --> 28:29.583
If there was just a small crack
to breathe through, I could live.

28:30.208 --> 28:34.421
I guess I wanted that pen
to be that "if" for you.

28:36.757 --> 28:39.217
You became that "if" for me,

28:40.218 --> 28:43.096
because I started drawing again,
thanks to you.

28:44.932 --> 28:45.933
Hey, Chan.

28:46.433 --> 28:48.100
Got the dorm maintenance notice.

28:48.101 --> 28:49.311
Thank you.

28:50.395 --> 28:51.771
Wow, you're really good.

28:51.772 --> 28:53.856
You think you can draw me one day?

28:53.857 --> 28:56.317
Uh…  Okay.

28:56.318 --> 28:58.653
- Ah. Good, thanks.
-  And…

28:58.654 --> 29:01.656
for the first time,
I started looking forward to the next day.

29:01.657 --> 29:04.367
The moments I spent talking to you

29:04.368 --> 29:08.038
helped me stay strong
without crumbling down.

29:10.332 --> 29:11.333
:cue

29:11.875 --> 29:12.959
5. THE EXPLOSION

29:12.960 --> 29:14.043
But…

29:14.044 --> 29:18.214
near the end of that summer,
there was an accident.

29:18.215 --> 29:19.383
A lab explosion.

29:21.843 --> 29:25.262
Everyone said I'd die soon
and that I would never wake up.

29:25.263 --> 29:26.347
But…

29:26.348 --> 29:27.391
Chan.

29:27.683 --> 29:28.766
I heard a voice.

29:28.767 --> 29:30.142
I love you.

29:31.311 --> 29:32.770
I love you, Chan.

29:32.771 --> 29:36.108
It was as if that voice
was trying to wake me up.

29:37.776 --> 29:39.778
I woke to that voice,

29:41.321 --> 29:42.614
but I couldn't remember

29:43.240 --> 29:45.909
who called my name and woke me up.

29:48.412 --> 29:50.956
I lost my memories after the accident
for about a year,

29:51.957 --> 29:54.292
but for some reason,

29:55.085 --> 29:56.628
that person's face and voice

29:57.212 --> 30:01.216
kept popping up vividly in my mind.

30:02.009 --> 30:05.512
And when I came to Korea for treatment,
I spotted her by coincidence.

30:06.555 --> 30:07.806
On Christmas Eve,

30:08.515 --> 30:09.808
at Jamsugyo.

30:10.434 --> 30:11.976
I ran after her,

30:11.977 --> 30:15.105
thinking she'd be the one
holding the key to my memories.

30:18.483 --> 30:22.070
But fireworks suddenly went off,
and I remembered the explosion.

30:22.487 --> 30:24.030
All my hazy memories

30:24.031 --> 30:26.366
came flooding back.

30:27.993 --> 30:29.119
That's when I realized

30:29.911 --> 30:33.540
that person
was my old roommate's girlfriend,

30:34.291 --> 30:35.417
and that I was just…

30:36.376 --> 30:40.963
a complete stranger to you.

30:46.887 --> 30:48.220
6. MEMENTO MORI

30:48.221 --> 30:50.556
I immediately left
without a clear destination.

30:50.557 --> 30:52.183
I wanted to get rid of my past.

30:52.184 --> 30:54.226
I'd like a ticket
for the earliest departure anywhere.

30:54.227 --> 30:57.439
But there was one thing
I just couldn't get rid of.

31:00.609 --> 31:03.402
There was someone
who had helped me survive twice.

31:03.403 --> 31:04.487
DRAW

31:04.488 --> 31:06.155
At least for her sake,

31:06.156 --> 31:08.825
I knew I had to stop
living like a dead person.

31:09.409 --> 31:12.954
I got this tattoo
so I wouldn't forget that resolution.

31:13.538 --> 31:14.831
"Memento Mori."

31:17.292 --> 31:22.130
So I struggled for seven years
like I was trying to become someone else,

31:22.672 --> 31:24.173
and at some point,

31:24.174 --> 31:27.176
my environment, surroundings, and I…

31:27.177 --> 31:29.054
had really changed.

31:29.846 --> 31:32.765
It was as if my past did not matter.

31:34.184 --> 31:36.436
7. NICE TO MEET YOU

31:37.687 --> 31:41.273
Then one day, you appeared again

31:41.274 --> 31:44.318
right in front of me, after seven years.

31:44.319 --> 31:45.653
It's nice to meet you.

31:45.654 --> 31:47.863
I'm Song Haran, the lead designer.

31:47.864 --> 31:50.241
I thought I was going to cry.

31:50.242 --> 31:53.828
I was so grateful, and I missed you
and was curious about you, but…

31:53.829 --> 31:55.831
It's nice to meet you. I'm…

31:56.498 --> 31:59.500
You were someone
I shouldn't even think about.

31:59.501 --> 32:00.918
…Seonu Chan.

32:00.919 --> 32:02.461
8. LET'S HAVE FUN LIKE A SPRING PICNIC

32:03.547 --> 32:05.589
If anything happens to you too…

32:05.590 --> 32:06.591
Haran.

32:07.259 --> 32:11.138
At first, I decided to avoid you
so I wouldn't get caught,

32:12.889 --> 32:14.391
but I felt pained

32:15.433 --> 32:16.434
while watching you.

32:18.103 --> 32:21.773
The person who saved me seven years ago
was trapped alone in winter.

32:23.817 --> 32:25.484
I thought I'd regret it later…

32:25.485 --> 32:27.653
It's really valuable to me,
so I have to find it.

32:27.654 --> 32:29.406
So I ended up making a crazy offer.

32:30.365 --> 32:31.657
A three-month trial!

32:31.658 --> 32:33.325
Then let's do this.

32:33.326 --> 32:35.120
It'll be like we're on a spring picnic.

32:35.871 --> 32:36.872
Let's have fun.
:cue

32:46.423 --> 32:48.132
9. GREED

32:48.133 --> 32:51.510
Many things happened between us
after that.

32:59.019 --> 33:01.520
Tell me if it keeps hurting.

33:01.521 --> 33:03.106
I'll carry you if I have to.

33:03.607 --> 33:04.649
Ms. Song!

33:07.319 --> 33:08.653
How have you been?

33:13.658 --> 33:14.951
This is bad.

33:25.086 --> 33:27.254
I ended up liking you so much,

33:27.255 --> 33:30.508
even when
I couldn't explain myself to you.

33:36.848 --> 33:40.100
10. MY BIRTHDAY, THE DAY I DECIDED
TO EXPLAIN MYSELF DESPITE THE GAPS

33:41.478 --> 33:44.563
I feel like
telling you everything today, too.

33:44.564 --> 33:47.483
I think I should stop
hiding things about myself.

33:47.484 --> 33:48.609
Odd or even?

33:48.610 --> 33:50.946
- I wanted to tell you everything…
- Odd.

33:52.656 --> 33:55.199
But I knew my memories
weren't fully intact.

33:56.284 --> 33:58.161
I grew worried that acting rashly

33:59.704 --> 34:03.375
would ruin things between us
or hurt you in some way.

34:03.833 --> 34:05.085
And in spring…

34:05.669 --> 34:07.671
Will you not be here in spring?

34:08.421 --> 34:12.675
I'm going to use that trial
for the rest of my life.

34:12.676 --> 34:13.801
But…

34:13.802 --> 34:15.386
I felt frustrated

34:15.387 --> 34:18.682
that I couldn't talk about the future
with the person I loved.

34:19.599 --> 34:22.018
So I made a decision.

34:22.394 --> 34:26.522
I decided I'd slowly explain
what I could remember.

34:26.523 --> 34:29.317
Do you have time after the movie?

34:29.734 --> 34:31.528
There's something I have to tell you.

34:32.612 --> 34:34.823
I knew you would see

34:35.699 --> 34:37.075
how sincere I was.

34:42.289 --> 34:43.540
I wanted to show you

34:44.165 --> 34:45.875
that there's another way.

34:46.584 --> 34:48.877
I learned it through that person.

34:48.878 --> 34:51.964
She was just
someone who broadened my world.

34:51.965 --> 34:53.925
You felt like someone you miss

34:54.759 --> 34:56.677
called your name.

34:56.678 --> 35:00.181
You already did that for me.

35:05.020 --> 35:08.273
I thought it would be impossible,
so I scribbled it out…

35:13.737 --> 35:15.237
but it might be possible now.

35:17.907 --> 35:19.450
He went traveling with me.

35:19.451 --> 35:22.578
Hyeokchan was away during vacation
to help our professor.

35:22.579 --> 35:24.372
He asked me for a favor.

35:27.709 --> 35:29.293
I chose to never do anything

35:29.294 --> 35:32.630
that might get in the way
of her happiness.

35:32.631 --> 35:35.174
Thanks to you, I just realized

35:35.175 --> 35:38.970
that not digging up old wounds
is also a way

35:40.472 --> 35:42.849
of protecting their happiness.

35:44.976 --> 35:46.102
That was all about me.

35:55.153 --> 35:57.197
I should've heard him out.

35:57.989 --> 35:59.866
I should've listened to him just once.
:cue

36:17.300 --> 36:18.635
-  Is this okay?
-  Let me see.

36:19.135 --> 36:20.762
Good.

36:22.639 --> 36:24.348
Your discharge is complete.

36:24.349 --> 36:25.683
Congratulations.

36:25.684 --> 36:26.768
- Great.
- Let's go.

36:29.062 --> 36:30.896
-  Mr. Park is here.
- Ta-da.

36:30.897 --> 36:31.980
Here.

36:31.981 --> 36:34.858
- He's here.
- Congratulations on your discharge.

36:34.859 --> 36:36.277
They're beautiful.

36:36.736 --> 36:39.530
Let me give you a ride back.
I'll drop you off at SHIM.

36:39.531 --> 36:41.991
Manjae. Should we walk back?

36:42.951 --> 36:44.451
I want to take a walk.

36:44.452 --> 36:48.122
I want to breathe in the cold air
and the smell of winter.

36:48.123 --> 36:49.748
You'll catch a cold outside.

36:49.749 --> 36:50.916
Just take our car.

36:50.917 --> 36:53.043
They're right. You should get some rest.

36:53.044 --> 36:55.087
A winter walk?

36:55.088 --> 36:58.006
That sounds amazing.

37:10.270 --> 37:11.271
It's amazing.

37:12.564 --> 37:16.984
I thought walking and breathing

37:16.985 --> 37:19.070
were just natural things in life,

37:21.239 --> 37:22.240
but today,

37:23.324 --> 37:24.492
it all feels like a gift.

37:27.871 --> 37:29.205
I realized that too late.

37:31.166 --> 37:33.084
Seeing such a beautiful sunset

37:34.419 --> 37:35.795
and feeling the seasons…

37:37.046 --> 37:38.256
I could have always

37:39.215 --> 37:40.216
lived…

37:41.509 --> 37:43.719
like life was a gift if I wanted to.

37:43.720 --> 37:45.679
It's not late at all.

37:45.680 --> 37:46.681
From now on,

37:47.974 --> 37:50.727
we can do it all together,
little by little.

37:58.860 --> 38:00.194
In the meantime,

38:00.195 --> 38:03.781
we went through big and small changes.

38:03.782 --> 38:04.907
No need to hurry.

38:04.908 --> 38:06.117
- One at a time.
- Slowly…

38:06.951 --> 38:08.202
Good job.

38:08.203 --> 38:09.245
Almost there.

38:13.333 --> 38:14.375
Yougyum.

38:15.251 --> 38:16.585
What is it, Hadam?

38:20.340 --> 38:22.132
"Congratulations, you've been…"

38:24.344 --> 38:27.263
- Hadam!
- I'm a real med student now!

38:27.764 --> 38:29.473
Great job, Hadam.

38:29.474 --> 38:31.099
I can't believe it.

38:31.100 --> 38:33.519
Yougyum, what's going on?
Why are you jumping?

38:33.520 --> 38:36.563
Hadam's a med student now.

38:36.564 --> 38:38.899
She just got accepted.

38:42.278 --> 38:45.030
Hey. Why are you crying?

38:45.031 --> 38:46.448
You're not her boyfriend.

38:46.449 --> 38:48.200
I just got a call from the team.

38:48.201 --> 38:50.954
I thought it was over
after I went undrafted,

38:51.496 --> 38:53.540
but I got picked up by the Taesan Titans.

38:54.374 --> 38:56.041
I'm going pro!

38:56.042 --> 38:57.709
- Wow.
- Hey.

38:57.710 --> 38:58.961
Yang Changmo!

39:01.923 --> 39:02.924
Hang on.

39:03.550 --> 39:05.426
Hey, how am I jumping?

39:06.928 --> 39:08.720
Oh? It doesn't hurt.

39:08.721 --> 39:09.722
Really?

39:10.223 --> 39:11.473
It really doesn't hurt?

39:11.474 --> 39:12.725
No, not at all.

39:13.643 --> 39:16.979
It doesn't hurt!

39:16.980 --> 39:18.189
Sir! Mr. Cha!

39:18.773 --> 39:20.190
You shouldn't jump yet.

39:20.191 --> 39:21.776
Sorry.

39:24.529 --> 39:26.865
:cue

39:32.370 --> 39:33.371
Are you heading out?

39:34.289 --> 39:36.541
Yes, I'm heading out.

39:40.920 --> 39:44.548
He said he has feelings for me.

39:44.549 --> 39:47.843
He asked if he could like me,
and I said yes.

39:47.844 --> 39:50.137
But he's exactly the same as before…

39:50.138 --> 39:52.807
If you're free,
would you like to have some wine?

39:54.225 --> 39:56.894
Just the two of us.

39:56.895 --> 39:59.522
Just the two of us?

40:02.275 --> 40:03.734
All right.

40:03.735 --> 40:06.070
Sounds good.

40:17.248 --> 40:18.373
What is this?

40:18.374 --> 40:21.209
You just got surgery.
You need to regain your strength.

40:21.210 --> 40:24.922
It's a local specialty from Jeju,
made by a master artisan. They're tasty.

40:24.923 --> 40:26.882
- Mmm.
- Have them with your granddaughters.

40:26.883 --> 40:28.842
- They look delicious. Manjae.
- Yes?

40:28.843 --> 40:30.178
You should have some too.

40:34.223 --> 40:37.726
All right. They look delicious.

40:37.727 --> 40:39.269
Okay.

40:39.270 --> 40:40.647
-  Eat up.
-  Okay.

40:40.772 --> 40:42.314
Focus on recovering.

40:42.315 --> 40:44.441
- You should eat too.
- All right.

40:44.442 --> 40:45.859
-  Here.
-  Eat up, everyone.

40:45.860 --> 40:47.612
Thank you.

40:50.615 --> 40:51.698
Goodness.

40:51.699 --> 40:54.326
Mmm! They're so chewy.

40:54.327 --> 40:55.869
-  Good.
- They're so tasty.

40:55.870 --> 40:57.246
This is good.

40:58.122 --> 40:59.623
Mmm. It's delicious.

40:59.624 --> 41:01.750
"This was the email
from the Comets."

41:01.751 --> 41:04.586
"We watched the medical test video."

41:04.587 --> 41:06.546
"We would like to verify

41:06.547 --> 41:09.508
his rehabilitation progress
and other aspects besides the video,

41:09.509 --> 41:12.427
so we suggest conducting a final test

41:12.428 --> 41:16.265
at a local training center
as soon as possible."

41:17.141 --> 41:18.225
What?

41:18.226 --> 41:20.185
You have to go to the States for the test?

41:20.186 --> 41:22.981
They must be worried because of my injury.

41:24.190 --> 41:26.192
I'll go and try my best until the end.

41:26.693 --> 41:29.361
As you said, if I give up
without trying until the end,

41:29.362 --> 41:31.488
all that will be left is regret.

41:31.489 --> 41:32.490
All right.

41:32.949 --> 41:36.034
Go and show them everything you've got,

41:36.035 --> 41:37.161
and leave no regrets.

41:40.957 --> 41:42.000
Let's do this!

41:42.500 --> 41:43.501
Let's do this!

41:44.127 --> 41:45.128
Gather our strength.

41:45.753 --> 41:48.505
-  After many things happened…
- You can do it, right?

41:48.506 --> 41:49.716
…during fall and winter,

41:50.383 --> 41:52.885
the seasons passed…

41:56.264 --> 41:57.807
It really is spring.

41:58.641 --> 42:00.308
And winter began to meet...

42:00.309 --> 42:02.645
...the beginning of spring.

42:04.981 --> 42:09.860
However, the man who offered
a fun spring picnic

42:09.861 --> 42:13.530
was nowhere to be found in spring.

42:13.531 --> 42:15.699
- I really wanted something cold.
- Wow.

42:15.700 --> 42:17.826
This is heaven.
It's so hot outside.

42:17.827 --> 42:18.910
Here.

42:18.911 --> 42:20.705
-  Thank you.
-  This is insane.

42:23.666 --> 42:25.710
Let's go see
the cherry blossoms in spring.

42:26.210 --> 42:27.420
We'll have…

42:29.047 --> 42:30.631
shaved ice in summer.

42:31.841 --> 42:33.175
Have some, Ms. Song.

42:33.176 --> 42:34.468
Come and have one.

42:34.469 --> 42:36.636
I'm okay. Enjoy.

42:36.637 --> 42:39.389
Even as another season passed,

42:39.390 --> 42:41.768
there was still no news from him.

42:42.935 --> 42:44.353
:cue

42:55.740 --> 43:00.286
GERANIUM
I CAN'T STOP THINKING OF YOU

43:24.227 --> 43:25.435
It's that cloud, right?

43:25.436 --> 43:27.646
The one that Ms. Song saw in Gyeongju

43:27.647 --> 43:30.607
that was the inspiration for Won's outfit.

43:30.608 --> 43:31.775
What was it called?

43:31.776 --> 43:33.820
- An iridescent cloud.
-  That's right.

43:35.238 --> 43:37.155
It's called an iridescent cloud.

43:37.156 --> 43:39.659
They say you have good luck
if you see an iridescent cloud.

43:41.119 --> 43:42.536
Come to think of it,

43:42.537 --> 43:45.580
it's already been a year
since we went to Gyeongju.

43:45.581 --> 43:46.706
I uploaded it.

43:46.707 --> 43:49.000
Everyone, like my post.

43:49.001 --> 43:52.547
Hey, Song Haran.
I'm not letting you slip away quietly.

43:53.965 --> 43:55.508
Give me a like on my feed.

44:12.483 --> 44:14.068
Here's a lucky charm.

44:14.735 --> 44:17.613
You know you'll get lucky
once you see an iridescent cloud.

44:21.576 --> 44:25.745
WE'RE USING THE DRAWING YOU GIFTED US
FOR OUR WEDDING INVITES!

44:28.416 --> 44:31.085
IRIDESCENT CLOUD ARTIST

44:36.340 --> 44:39.593
I JUST GOT A SURPRISE DRAWING GIFT
THANK YOU FOR THE GREAT MEMORY!

44:39.594 --> 44:42.220
"Gangneung, 16 minutes…"

44:42.221 --> 44:43.513
16 MINUTES AGO

44:43.514 --> 44:47.934
I… I'm taking the afternoon off.

44:47.935 --> 44:49.103
That's so sudden.

44:49.896 --> 44:50.897
What?

44:51.689 --> 44:52.856
She just got here, though.

45:05.536 --> 45:06.579
Hello.

45:07.163 --> 45:09.874
You looked so happy,
so I drew a picture of you.

45:10.374 --> 45:11.459
Can I gift it to you?

45:13.836 --> 45:15.503
- You're giving this to us?
-  Yes.

45:15.504 --> 45:16.505
Thank you.

45:18.674 --> 45:19.926
But what's this cloud?

45:20.635 --> 45:22.177
It's an iridescent cloud.

45:22.178 --> 45:24.095
They say it gives you good luck.

45:24.096 --> 45:26.139
I wanted to wish you fortune.

45:26.140 --> 45:27.600
Enjoy your trip.

45:28.351 --> 45:29.727
Thank you.

45:31.312 --> 45:33.147
You're here.

45:33.606 --> 45:34.649
It's so pretty.

45:55.628 --> 45:57.337
This is your sign, right?

45:57.338 --> 46:01.549
Have you seen anyone nearby
who draws pictures like this?

46:01.550 --> 46:02.676
I'm not sure.

46:02.677 --> 46:04.970
Have you seen anyone
who draws pictures like this?

46:04.971 --> 46:06.054
No.

46:06.055 --> 46:10.267
Hello, have you seen
an artist drawing pictures nearby?

46:10.268 --> 46:11.310
No.

46:13.104 --> 46:14.938
Excuse me,
can I ask you something?

46:14.939 --> 46:18.400
Have you seen an artist
who draws pictures with a cloud like this?

46:18.401 --> 46:19.859
We received one earlier.
:cue

46:19.860 --> 46:21.361
Isn't it this cloud?

46:21.362 --> 46:24.114
When did you see him?

46:24.115 --> 46:25.407
Just earlier today.

46:25.408 --> 46:27.159
- Four or five hours ago.
- Okay.

46:27.994 --> 46:30.121
Thank you.

46:57.982 --> 47:00.151
Where on earth did he go?

47:14.957 --> 47:16.208
Mmm.

47:21.422 --> 47:23.048
- Hello.
-  Hello.

47:23.049 --> 47:24.341
What a cool dog.

47:24.342 --> 47:25.968
- Can I pet it?
- Sure.

47:27.386 --> 47:28.928
Hi.

47:28.929 --> 47:31.181
I was close to a dog
that looked just like this one.

47:31.182 --> 47:32.183
Really?

47:33.309 --> 47:34.310
Bye.

47:35.186 --> 47:36.228
Bye.

48:00.753 --> 48:01.962
Sorry.

48:03.297 --> 48:05.174
I dropped my pen…

48:06.300 --> 48:07.385
again.

48:28.614 --> 48:29.615
I found you.

48:34.537 --> 48:36.163
I found you, Seonu Chan.

48:37.623 --> 48:38.706
Why?

48:38.707 --> 48:40.751
Why were you here alone?

48:45.131 --> 48:47.550
I'm sorry, I realized too late.

48:50.302 --> 48:52.513
Thank you for lying for me.

48:54.557 --> 48:57.268
Thank you for protecting my scars.

48:59.895 --> 49:02.188
No, it's all my fault.

49:02.189 --> 49:04.775
I wasn't the only one
who didn't know what happened.

49:05.484 --> 49:07.695
There are things you didn't know, either.

49:08.696 --> 49:09.780
It's all my fault.

49:10.531 --> 49:12.783
- I was being greedy--
-  No.

49:13.409 --> 49:15.244
You didn't cause that accident.

49:16.245 --> 49:17.955
Dr. Cha told me everything.

49:19.832 --> 49:22.792
Seonu Chan disappeared because of me.

49:22.793 --> 49:24.170
It was Hyeokchan

49:25.212 --> 49:26.589
who caused the explosion.

49:28.841 --> 49:30.634
And Seonu Chan was just a victim.

49:31.677 --> 49:32.887
I lied to him.

49:34.221 --> 49:37.475
I wanted to protect Hyeokchan
in any way I could.
:cue

49:41.645 --> 49:43.563
I'm sorry, it was me--

49:43.564 --> 49:45.191
It was caused by his lighter.

49:45.900 --> 49:48.359
It happened because Hyeokchan
turned his lighter on.

49:56.535 --> 49:58.453
Why would you
ruin everything like this?

49:58.454 --> 49:59.537
Stop it, Hyeokchan.

49:59.538 --> 50:00.664
Tell me!

50:01.290 --> 50:02.499
You have to remember.

50:02.500 --> 50:04.668
None of it was your fault.

50:05.503 --> 50:08.379
You've been talking to Haran
while I was away?

50:08.380 --> 50:09.923
Pretending to be me? Why?

50:09.924 --> 50:12.592
Did you think it was okay
since I asked you a few times?

50:12.593 --> 50:14.970
You were someone nobody even cared about.

50:16.305 --> 50:18.806
Did you get excited

50:18.807 --> 50:20.434
that someone paid attention to you?

50:20.935 --> 50:22.143
Kang Hyeokchan!

50:22.144 --> 50:23.979
You never hit Hyeokchan.

50:29.068 --> 50:30.778
It was…

50:40.162 --> 50:41.455
…Hyeokchan who hit you.

50:42.164 --> 50:43.832
Tell me!

50:44.291 --> 50:46.084
Kang Hyeokchan!

50:51.048 --> 50:53.092
I have something to tell you.

50:53.884 --> 50:54.927
Your messenger…

50:55.219 --> 50:56.220
What?

50:58.097 --> 50:59.640
While I was using your laptop,

51:00.140 --> 51:03.352
I kept chatting with your girlfriend.

51:07.731 --> 51:08.857
What?

51:11.068 --> 51:13.362
What are you talking about?
Say that again.

51:14.446 --> 51:15.906
We ended up

51:16.991 --> 51:18.284
chatting after that.

51:19.451 --> 51:22.121
But she thinks it was you.

51:24.164 --> 51:26.792
Hyeokchan,
you left your earphones in my car…

51:28.961 --> 51:29.962
Are you saying

51:30.588 --> 51:34.967
you've been talking to Haran
while I was away?

51:35.426 --> 51:36.427
Pretending to be me?

51:39.805 --> 51:40.848
Sorry.

51:45.227 --> 51:46.228
Hang on.

51:47.938 --> 51:49.023
Who are you to do that?

51:49.565 --> 51:52.985
Why would you ruin everything like this?

51:53.277 --> 51:56.779
I was already feeling guilty

51:56.780 --> 51:58.865
and wondering how to end things.

51:58.866 --> 52:00.868
My head was already about to explode.

52:02.202 --> 52:03.954
Do you have any idea what you've done?

52:07.875 --> 52:08.876
I'm sorry.

52:09.960 --> 52:11.003
Tell me.

52:12.838 --> 52:15.382
What sort of things have you been saying?

52:17.801 --> 52:19.511
Tell me!

52:23.140 --> 52:24.475
Kang Hyeokchan!

52:27.353 --> 52:30.480
Who are you to take away
my chance to end things peacefully?

52:30.481 --> 52:33.524
What am I supposed to do now?

52:33.525 --> 52:34.818
Why?

52:35.277 --> 52:37.904
Did you think it was okay
since I asked you a few times?

52:37.905 --> 52:40.199
You were someone nobody even cared about.

52:40.824 --> 52:42.618
Did you get excited

52:44.662 --> 52:46.163
that someone paid attention to you?

52:47.164 --> 52:48.707
Stop it, Hyeokchan.

52:49.416 --> 52:51.835
You're the one
who's been bad to your girlfriend.

52:52.461 --> 52:53.587
No, it's us.

52:54.004 --> 52:55.255
And you stopped liking her.

52:55.673 --> 52:57.341
So don't take it out on your roommate.

53:02.513 --> 53:04.138
You should leave for a moment.

53:14.483 --> 53:16.235
Are you crazy? We're in a lab.

53:16.694 --> 53:18.237
You're smoking too much these days.

53:18.946 --> 53:20.071
Watch yourself.

53:23.909 --> 53:25.119
Here for pickup.

53:29.164 --> 53:31.083
Never leave the waste container like this.

53:31.583 --> 53:34.085
Even a small leak will set off the sensor.

53:34.086 --> 53:35.461
Be careful.

53:35.462 --> 53:37.756
Sorry. I will.

53:39.007 --> 53:42.343
The waste container had
nothing to do with the accident either,

53:42.344 --> 53:43.887
because they collected it right away.

53:44.763 --> 53:46.264
I was a witness.

53:49.643 --> 53:50.769
It's not too late.

53:52.896 --> 53:55.691
Go back to Korea and meet your girlfriend.

53:56.734 --> 53:59.527
Explain everything to her
and apologize properly.

53:59.528 --> 54:01.320
And apologize to your roommate.

54:01.321 --> 54:02.613
You're the one

54:02.614 --> 54:04.866
who took his laptop
and asked him to cover for you.

54:04.867 --> 54:05.950
:cue

54:05.951 --> 54:07.286
You're in a dangerous state.

54:07.745 --> 54:10.705
Just go and get some rest.
I'll get going now.

54:23.927 --> 54:25.970
Chan, I saw a vapor trail earlier.

54:25.971 --> 54:28.556
But that made me want
to get on a plane to go see you.

54:48.827 --> 54:50.578
It wasn't your fault.

54:50.579 --> 54:53.539
The one who made me want to rush over

54:53.540 --> 54:55.000
and say "I love you"

54:55.417 --> 54:56.876
was you, back then and now.

55:09.181 --> 55:10.307
I love you.

55:10.807 --> 55:12.226
I love you, Seonu Chan.

56:16.873 --> 56:17.916
Oh, no.

56:21.545 --> 56:23.422
Where did he go?

56:24.006 --> 56:25.464
The detailed exam confirmed

56:25.465 --> 56:28.301
the shrapnel had shifted
and was stimulating his nerves.

56:28.302 --> 56:31.053
It caused memory disturbance
and hallucinations.

56:31.054 --> 56:33.431
Luckily, it shifted
to an operable position,

56:33.432 --> 56:35.392
so we were able to remove the shrapnel.

56:36.852 --> 56:38.020
Song Haran.

56:40.439 --> 56:42.398
But due to severe mental fatigue,

56:42.399 --> 56:44.860
he hasn't been able to wake up
for several days.

56:58.165 --> 57:01.043
We'll have to wait until he wakes up

57:02.044 --> 57:04.171
to see how the surgery
will affect his memories.

57:15.807 --> 57:16.974
Every time I see you,

57:16.975 --> 57:20.061
I swallow the same words
stuck in my throat.

57:20.062 --> 57:21.688
11. WHAT I WANT TO TELL YOU

57:25.233 --> 57:26.234
But…

57:26.652 --> 57:27.986
I won't swallow them anymore.

57:29.029 --> 57:31.657
I'm going to tell you
when I meet you today.

57:33.158 --> 57:34.950
The words I decided to say to you

57:34.951 --> 57:37.286
the moment my memories
were fully recovered.

57:40.082 --> 57:41.166
I love you.

57:46.338 --> 57:50.384
I LOVE YOU
I LOVE YOU, SONG HARAN

58:10.821 --> 58:12.781
I love you, Song Haran.

58:16.868 --> 58:18.537
:cue

59:29.024 --> 59:31.150
Music start!

59:49.961 --> 59:51.379
Congratulations!

59:59.054 --> 01:00:00.347
Congratulations!

01:00:23.328 --> 01:00:24.329
Okay.

01:00:46.101 --> 01:00:47.893
Kiss!

01:00:47.894 --> 01:00:50.980
- Kiss.
- Kiss.

01:00:50.981 --> 01:00:53.649
Kiss.

01:00:53.650 --> 01:00:54.901
Kiss…

01:01:03.743 --> 01:01:05.996
Oh, my gosh!
He really did it!

01:01:10.750 --> 01:01:12.711
Congratulations.

01:01:34.524 --> 01:01:35.816
Here.

01:01:35.817 --> 01:01:37.861
What? A baseball?

01:01:39.029 --> 01:01:41.947
The ball from my final strikeout
that got me my first win.

01:01:41.948 --> 01:01:43.491
I wanted to give it to you.

01:01:44.326 --> 01:01:46.786
I know I'm still in the minor leagues.

01:01:48.038 --> 01:01:49.039
Thank you, Hadam.

01:01:49.497 --> 01:01:51.165
For not letting me give up.

01:01:51.166 --> 01:01:54.628
Thank you for not giving up until the end.

01:01:57.923 --> 01:01:59.798
But now that I think about it,

01:01:59.799 --> 01:02:02.509
- we were so immature.
- What?

01:02:02.510 --> 01:02:04.845
We thought we'd feel too anxious
being apart,

01:02:04.846 --> 01:02:06.931
so we thought
marriage was our only option.

01:02:08.391 --> 01:02:13.020
But now, no matter how far apart we are,
I don't feel anxious at all.

01:02:13.021 --> 01:02:15.856
Right. I don't feel anxious at all.

01:02:17.567 --> 01:02:20.153
Have we… matured?

01:02:23.406 --> 01:02:25.617
Keep up with your rehab
during the offseason

01:02:26.076 --> 01:02:28.953
and get yourself in perfect shape
before the spring camp.

01:02:28.954 --> 01:02:30.038
Okay.

01:02:30.622 --> 01:02:31.623
And…

01:02:33.124 --> 01:02:34.458
sign this for me.

01:02:34.459 --> 01:02:36.252
I'm your number one fan, remember?

01:02:37.837 --> 01:02:38.838
I already signed it.

01:02:41.007 --> 01:02:43.802
TO MY NO. 1 DOCTOR HADAM
I'M ALWAYS ROOTING FOR YOU, CHA YOUGYUM

01:02:48.306 --> 01:02:50.016
I'm your number one fan too.

01:02:53.853 --> 01:02:55.104
Hey!

01:02:55.105 --> 01:02:56.106
:cue

01:03:00.694 --> 01:03:03.821
-  Isn't B better?
-  Yes, B is better.

01:03:03.822 --> 01:03:04.906
Who prefers option A?

01:03:06.032 --> 01:03:08.200
What? It's 3 to 3?

01:03:08.201 --> 01:03:09.576
What should we do, then?

01:03:14.958 --> 01:03:15.959
C.

01:03:16.918 --> 01:03:17.919
Ms. Kim!

01:03:19.379 --> 01:03:20.797
Ms. Kim is here.

01:03:22.007 --> 01:03:23.842
When you're not sure about both A and B,

01:03:24.259 --> 01:03:25.843
- then it's C.
-  But, Ms. Kim,

01:03:25.844 --> 01:03:29.138
you said you'd take a year off
with Mr. Park in France.

01:03:29.139 --> 01:03:32.474
A month was enough.
Taking a long break isn't my thing.

01:03:32.475 --> 01:03:36.520
All right, then I'll be expecting
an upgraded option.

01:03:36.521 --> 01:03:38.856
- Okay.
- Yes, Ms. Kim.

01:03:38.857 --> 01:03:40.524
All right, then.

01:03:40.525 --> 01:03:42.860
Let's prepare option C.

01:03:42.861 --> 01:03:43.944
Let's begin.

01:03:43.945 --> 01:03:45.279
-  Let's do this.
-  Clean this.

01:03:45.280 --> 01:03:46.364
Let's do this!

01:03:48.491 --> 01:03:50.410
Are you heading out now, Ms. Song?

01:03:51.077 --> 01:03:53.830
Congratulations on the bio-silk reorder.

01:03:54.581 --> 01:03:57.541
Right. Thank you so much.

01:03:57.542 --> 01:03:59.543
Is there something wrong?

01:03:59.544 --> 01:04:01.920
Even outside the office,

01:04:01.921 --> 01:04:03.964
you're always calling me Ms. Song.

01:04:03.965 --> 01:04:04.966
Nothing's changed…

01:04:06.801 --> 01:04:08.302
Forget it.

01:04:08.303 --> 01:04:11.764
Ms. Song Hayeong will head home now,

01:04:11.765 --> 01:04:13.349
COO Yeon Taeseok.

01:04:17.896 --> 01:04:19.104
Hayeong.

01:04:32.702 --> 01:04:35.038
Do you have to go home early today?

01:04:35.622 --> 01:04:38.958
If I don't, then…

01:04:40.210 --> 01:04:41.543
I mean,

01:04:41.544 --> 01:04:44.631
it would be nice to have dinner
and watch a movie.

01:04:46.674 --> 01:04:48.425
That sounds good.

01:04:48.426 --> 01:04:50.178
I like movies.

01:04:51.596 --> 01:04:52.722
Let's go.

01:04:55.433 --> 01:04:56.810
- This way.
-  Okay!

01:05:06.402 --> 01:05:10.072
Oh? What's that face?
You'd better not draw me weird.

01:05:10.073 --> 01:05:11.990
Come on. I'm Seonu Chan.

01:05:11.991 --> 01:05:13.409
Don't you know my skills?

01:05:14.077 --> 01:05:15.160
All done.

01:05:15.161 --> 01:05:16.788
Oh. Hang on. Give me just 10 seconds.

01:05:19.624 --> 01:05:22.460
Let's close our eyes
and exchange them on the count of three.

01:05:23.211 --> 01:05:25.463
One, two, three.

01:05:25.964 --> 01:05:27.841
Oh! You're pretty good.

01:05:28.299 --> 01:05:30.467
Why aren't you showing me yours?

01:05:30.468 --> 01:05:33.471
Ah. I forgot. Can you count again?

01:05:34.305 --> 01:05:35.597
All right.

01:05:35.598 --> 01:05:37.600
One, two, three.

01:05:57.996 --> 01:06:01.583
Let's go see cherry blossoms in spring,

01:06:02.167 --> 01:06:04.210
eat shaved ice in summer,

01:06:04.711 --> 01:06:06.128
see the autumn leaves in fall,

01:06:06.129 --> 01:06:09.548
and go snowboarding in winter.

01:06:09.549 --> 01:06:10.758
Will you share

01:06:11.467 --> 01:06:13.261
every season of life with me

01:06:15.221 --> 01:06:16.306
from now on?

01:06:27.275 --> 01:06:29.694
You should stand up to match the drawing.

01:06:30.361 --> 01:06:31.988
Huh?

01:06:33.740 --> 01:06:34.741
Hmm.

01:06:56.304 --> 01:06:59.097
Thank you for appearing in my life.
:cue

01:06:59.098 --> 01:07:00.350
I told you,

01:07:00.975 --> 01:07:02.602
I'll appear anywhere for you.

01:07:05.188 --> 01:07:06.855
Thank you

01:07:06.856 --> 01:07:08.316
for appearing

01:07:08.983 --> 01:07:11.611
in my life and in my winter.

01:07:46.229 --> 01:07:48.480
The cherry blossoms are beautiful.

01:07:50.149 --> 01:07:51.525
-  This looks delicious.
-  Here.

01:07:51.526 --> 01:07:53.319
-  Mm! Isn't it good?
- Mm!

01:08:09.502 --> 01:08:10.503
This is nice.

01:08:27.770 --> 01:08:28.895
Chan! Chan!

01:08:28.896 --> 01:08:30.856
I read somewhere

01:08:30.857 --> 01:08:33.525
that the seasons in life
don't come in order.

01:08:33.526 --> 01:08:36.321
What if winter suddenly comes to my life?

01:08:50.209 --> 01:08:52.045
It will pass one day.

01:08:52.587 --> 01:08:54.796
Even if winter feels endless,

01:08:54.797 --> 01:08:56.924
a spring breeze might blow someday

01:08:57.550 --> 01:08:59.886
once you keep fighting through it.

01:09:10.688 --> 01:09:12.689
I couldn't do that,

01:09:12.690 --> 01:09:14.942
so I probably won't be able to
send this message,

01:09:16.277 --> 01:09:18.487
but I hope that
when you're going through winter,

01:09:18.488 --> 01:09:21.908
a warm spring breeze blows by eventually

01:09:23.117 --> 01:09:26.245
and ends the painful season
before it gets too long.

01:09:26.954 --> 01:09:28.081
And…

01:09:29.207 --> 01:09:31.751
I hope that whatever season
you're going through,

01:09:33.211 --> 01:09:35.921
they're all radiant.

01:09:44.597 --> 01:09:46.557
IN YOUR RADIANT SEASON

01:10:29.559 --> 01:10:32.769
Thank you for watching.

01:10:32.770 --> 01:10:34.021
Be happy, everyone.

01:10:35.106 --> 01:10:36.858
Oh, no. It's over.

01:10:37.775 --> 01:10:40.026
What a radiant life it was.

01:10:40.027 --> 01:10:44.115
THANK YOU FOR WATCHING
IN YOUR RADIANT SEASON

